ImageViewer patch (docs/PLAN.md section 15, D-57): the Nikon ShotInfo offsets are read only inside the tag
Library: libraw 0.22.2
Fixes: CVE-2026-111272
Upstream: none yet: no fix on master or 0.22-stable as of 2026-10-21 (ours)
Remove when: a release fixes CVE-2026-111272 (OSV), or this patch no longer applies

parseNikonMakernote() read 4-byte values at fixed offsets of the ShotInfo tag (0x10, 0x84,
0x98, 0x9c, 0xa0) whatever the tag's length: a short tag in a crafted NEF read past its heap
buffer. A value past the tag's end now reads as 0, which the code already treats as absent.

diff --git a/src/metadata/nikon.cpp b/src/metadata/nikon.cpp
index ef16100b..1c874077 100644
--- a/src/metadata/nikon.cpp
+++ b/src/metadata/nikon.cpp
@@ -21,6 +21,15 @@ double sget_fixed32u (short _order, uchar *s);
 double AngleConversion_a (short _order, uchar *s);
 double AngleConversion (short _order, uchar *s);
 
+// The 4-byte value at offset in the ShotInfo tag (len bytes), 0 past its end
+// (CVE-2026-111272: the offsets below are fixed, the tag's length is not).
+static unsigned shotinfo_get4(short _order, uchar *buf, unsigned len,
+                              unsigned offset)
+{
+  return offset <= len && len - offset >= 4 ? sget4_order(_order, buf + offset)
+                                            : 0;
+}
